\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Prefix Sliding is a source-reported intervention}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{source-observation}

\p{Muennighoff et al. describe Prefix Sliding in Sections 2--5, Figures
6--9, and the Limitations section of \citet{Sections 2--5, Figures 6--9, and Limitations}{muennighoff2026prefixsliding}.
Their method preserves a prefix while sliding a recent attention window during
test-time scaling. The reported experiments change retained context and
runtime, and may also change rollout horizon and the training gradient
approximation. These are source observations, not a theorem of universal
speedup or capability.}

\p{The source studies named model and task configurations. It does not by
itself establish support expansion, latent capability acquisition, or a
deployment-shift guarantee.}
